# Text color & hierarchy

Use brightness to signal importance on every page. Never render a section as a flat
block of uniform white text.

Tiers (use the existing design tokens — do not hardcode hex):
- Headings / section titles → --text (#E8ECE9), brightest
- Body copy & lead sentences → --muted (#9AA4A0)
- Short labels, dates, captions → --text-dim (#6B7570) — short text ONLY, never full sentences
- --accent (#2DD4BF) → dates/kickers, links, hover & focus, chip borders. Never body text.

Rules:
- Two or three brightness levels per section, used consistently.
- Keep all real body copy at WCAG AA contrast (≥4.5:1). --muted is safe;
  --text-dim is for short labels/dates only.
- Prefer scannable structure over dense paragraphs; cap long columns around 60–70ch.
- Headings use Space Grotesk, body uses Inter. JetBrains Mono is for terminal
  accents, code, kicker labels (~/…) and dates only — not headings or body.
